claude: unchanged .mcp.json
claude: unchanged .claude/skills/lockssh/SKILL.md
claude: unchanged .lockssh/config.toml
Claude Code asks once whether to use the project MCP server "lockssh"; approve it.
The calls below answer within the console's policy and budgets, without a prompt.
Optional: to stop Claude Code prompting for them, add them to
"permissions.allow" in .claude/settings.local.json (personal) or
.claude/settings.json (shared):

  "mcp__lockssh__lockssh_status",
  "Bash(lockssh status:*)",
  "Bash(lockssh doctor:*)"

lockssh_run asks Claude Code each time: its allow-listed commands run on the host at once; other commands are decided on lockhub (lox approve, the lea deck or a paired phone).


